      },
      "message": "fix(slopbot): a fee dry run records no ask past the monthly review cap\n\nIn dry_run, gateSubmissionFee recorded an item row and a `recorded` gate\nfor every pull request the fee applies to, even when the monthly review\ncap would refuse the review. Live asks nothing in that case (PRD section 5:\n\"No fee is asked for a review that the intake cap or the monthly review cap\nwould refuse anyway\"), so the record of what live would ask was wrong, and\nthe stray item row is one the submission-fee Worker judges deposits against\nand the public item read lists as due.\n\nRecord only when `mayAsk` holds, as the live branch already requires. The\nQuint model's dry step follows the same rule and gains a run for it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
